From 513edf2e417699001899e5374ffab3d4664691e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 18:06:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: add a regression test that loads the output plugin

decoderbufs ships no test suite: there is no `sql/`, no `expected/`, and no
`REGRESS` in the Makefile, so a build has nothing to check beyond the fact
that the shared object linked. The plugin's own failure modes are exactly the
ones linking does not catch, above all an unresolved symbol or a missing
`_PG_output_plugin_init`, which only surface when the server dlopens it.

Being a logical-decoding output plugin, it has no SQL objects to exercise, so
the test does the one thing that proves the plugin is loadable and registered:
it opens a logical replication slot with it and drops it again. That is enough
to run `_PG_output_plugin_init` and the startup callback, whose `INFO` line the
transcript records.

`logical.conf` carries the server settings decoding needs (`wal_level =
logical` and slot/sender headroom), for a caller to pass to pg_regress as a
`--temp-config`, since a default instance cannot open a logical slot at all.
---
 logical.conf             | 3 +++
 sql/decoderbufs_load.sql | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 logical.conf
 create mode 100644 sql/decoderbufs_load.sql

diff --git a/logical.conf b/logical.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..107daf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/logical.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+wal_level = logical
+max_replication_slots = 10
+max_wal_senders = 10
diff --git a/sql/decoderbufs_load.sql b/sql/decoderbufs_load.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2562093
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sql/decoderbufs_load.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+-- decoderbufs is a logical-decoding output plugin with no SQL objects;
+-- verify the plugin loads and registers by opening a slot with it.
+SELECT slot_name FROM pg_create_logical_replication_slot('decoderbufs_test', 'decoderbufs');
+SELECT pg_drop_replication_slot('decoderbufs_test');
